 "description": "Gemini 4 Argon vs Gemini 3.8 Flash: 10 zero-shot coding challenges, same prompt, one attempt. Argon won 10-0 and took 39 minutes less.\n\nI tested Gemini 4 Argon and Gemini 3.8 Flash (High variants, inside Antigravity) with the same prompt on 10 challenges: 3D with Three.js, physics simulations, pixel art, pure CSS and math. Each model got a single attempt and delivered everything in one index.html, with no images or external models. Result: Argon 10-0 on quality and 55 versus 94 minutes in total (41.5% less), although Flash was faster in 3 challenges. The minutes come from my notes (rounded to the minute); the demos were recorded after generating.\n\nDEMOS AND CODE\nCode for all 20 projects: https://github.com/danpez/gemini-4-argon-vs-3.8-flash-benchmark\nPlayable demos (Argon and Flash): https://danpez.github.io/gemini-4-argon-vs-3.8-flash-benchmark/\n\nCHAPTERS\n00:00 The broken world\n00:18 Experiment protocol\n00:53 World 1, Level 1: Relative Solar System\n01:37 World 1, Level 2: 3D DNA Visualizer\n02:27 World 2, Level 3: Artificial Life\n03:05 World 2, Level 4: Dungeon Generator\n03:51 World 2, Level 5: Falling Sand Simulator\n04:35 World 3, Level 6: 3D Raycasting Engine, the boss\n05:33 World 3, Level 7: 8-Bit Space Sprites\n06:15 World 4, Level 8: CSS Analog Clock\n06:46 World 5, Level 9: Fractal Tree with Wind\n07:36 World 5, Level 10: Parametric Spirograph\n08:23 Results screen\n08:47 Lab verdict\n\nTOOLS\n- Voice: Voicefy, my own cloned voice, running locally on my Mac (narrated in English).\n- Editing and captions: Reelfy + Mixiuh Labs Studio (my own pipeline).\n- Music: original chiptune generated by code (no samples or third-party tracks).\n- Models: Gemini 4 Argon and Gemini 3.8 Flash (High variants) in Antigravity.\n\nThe narration uses my own cloned voice with Voicefy (runs locally).\n\n#Gemini4Argon #GeminiFlash #AI\n",
